 "fmea_markdown": "| Item | Failure mode | Effect | Detection | Severity [Y] | Mitigation | P per flight |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Seated sensor | stuck ACTIVE (reads seated) | open canopy shown as CANOPY UNLOCKED instead of OPEN; lock protection unchanged (bolt sensors) | functional test (ICA) | no safety effect | lock needs seated AND all bolts | 8.7e-06 |\n| Seated sensor | stuck INACTIVE | bolts sensed while 'not seated' -> CANOPY SENS caution (nuisance) | immediate (self-revealing) | minor | MEL/placard: system INOP, pilot handle check | 1.4e-07 |\n| Any sensor | open circuit / short | invalid complementary code -> CANOPY SENS, green off | immediate | minor | complementary outputs; fuselage-side harness only | 1.4e-07 |\n| Bolt sensor | stuck ACTIVE | that bolt unmonitored: a single-bolt hazard there is missed; a partial lock is still caught by the other two bolts (common linkage tube) | next powered opening (bolt sensed, canopy not seated) or functional test | major (latent) | three bolt sensors; plausibility check on every opening | 8.7e-06 |\n| Bolt sensor | stuck INACTIVE | false CANOPY UNLOCKED (nuisance) | immediate | minor | dispatch rule; fix before next flight | 1.4e-07 |\n| Bolt sensor | rigged to trip too early | partial lock read as locked (missed alert) | installation and annual go/no-go spacer test | major (latent) | rigging gauge in ICA; trip point set from tolerance study | — |\n| Bolt sensor | rigged to trip too late | full lock read as unlocked (false alarm) | immediate | minor | tolerance study; re-rig | — |\n| Alert unit | loss of power / CB open | panel dark, green LOCKED off, no alert | pilot checklist item 'CANOPY - LOCKED, green ON' | minor | positive-indication design | — |\n| Alert unit | logic error shows LOCKED | missed alert | functional test (ICA) | major (latent) | simple hardware AND for the green lamp; no software needed | — |\n| Red lamp / LED | fails dark | warning not seen (voice still works) | power-up lamp test | minor | two LEDs per legend; voice channel independent | — |\n| Voice / tone | no audio (headset unplugged) | warning only visual | power-up tone test | minor | flashing red in primary field of view | — |\n| Installation | part bridges canopy and fuselage | could obstruct emergency opening / jettison | ground test of emergency opening after installation | catastrophic if it occurred | nothing mounted across the split line; magnets passive in the frame | — |\n| Installation | magnet near the standby compass | compass deviation | compass swing | minor | magnet position and size; DO-160 magnetic-effect test | — |\n| Pilot | relies on the light, skips the handle check | the old barrier weakens | training / line checks | major | AFM supplement: handle check stays primary; system is supplementary | — |\n| Pilot | ignores alerts after nuisance alarms (cry wolf) | true alert not acted on | false-alarm monitoring in the event log | major | false-alarm budget; persistence filter | — |\n",
